<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis faithfully reproduces Helianthus annuus (sunflower capitulum) morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py, docs/media/vogel_phyllotaxis_growth.gif, vogel_phyllotaxis_metrics.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Helianthus annuus (sunflower capitulum) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 64.3/100, audit 2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit) and the assessments." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/vogel_phyllotaxis_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/vogel_phyllotaxis_metrics.csv; output: vogel_phyllotaxis_comparison.png; organism: Helianthus annuus (sunflower capitulum); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c; artifact_sha256: 98e2578361a0d0405b5a71cddc2f9ada03e666fcfb80e10ed5b14086a937b07d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/phyllotaxis/helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg=c76483eea3e564fe..., datasets/phyllotaxis/helianthus_parastichy_annotated.jpg=7cd34354e23584cb..., datasets/phyllotaxis/phyllotaxis_reference.json=432d1eeebf62bdc7...}; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Vogel (1979) defines planar capitulum spiral placement r_n = c*sqrt(n), theta_n = n*alpha_0 with golden divergence angle alpha_0 = 360/tau^2 = 137.507764 deg | Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) demonstrate self-organized convergence of repulsive Hofmeister primordia on a radially advecting meristem ring to the golden and Lucas noble angles | Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium (2016) report 768 photoreviewed parastichy counts across 657 Helianthus annuus heads (82.3% Fibonacci structure; 49 Fib-1 vs 17 Fib+1, binomial p = 3.3e-5); reconstructed_in_script: Planar Vogel spiral generator, Delaunay/Voronoi contact parastichy detector across concentric annuli, quasi-static Douady-Couder Hofmeister relaxation, and Swinton (2016) empirical survey comparison; transfer_boundary: Noisy divergence ensemble and bijugate whorl extensions used to compare model parastichy distributions with Swinton et al. (2016) Table 1; does_not_claim: In v1, floret centroids/parastichy modes are not yet extracted from the specimen photograph pixels, and Fib-1/Fib+1 grain defects are not yet produced by the noisy simulation ensemble]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0025-5564(79)90080-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.160091>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-specimen-match> ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.43e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Code-to-model traceability: 66/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Functions are clearly documented against paper sections, but the independent assessor caught three code-to-label mismatches: Panel E legend says initial angles 155/122/104 deg while code passes 175/130/99.8 deg; Panel C labels Sunflower 171 as (29,47) whereas JSON records (47,76); and Panel C CV labels were hardcoded rather than formatted from compute_packing_metrics(). Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L659–L665: Hardcoded CV strings and Sunflower 171 parastichy pair mismatch <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L659-L665>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L729–L738: Panel E legend initial angles vs function call arguments <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L729-L738>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Vogel's (1979) planar generative spiral r_n = c*sqrt(n), theta_n = n*alpha_0 and Delaunay rising Fibonacci parastichy cascade (8,13)->(13,21)->(21,34)->(34,55) are implemented accurately. Douady & Couder's (1992) Hofmeister inhibitory energy minimization converges to 137.59 deg (Fibonacci) and 99.38 deg (Lucas), though the Lucas branch is seeded near its basin (99.8 deg) rather than emerging purely from plastochron bifurcation. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L109–L155: vogel_spiral(): exact r_n = c*sqrt(n), theta_n = n*alpha_0 and J-jugate extension <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L109-L155>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L274–L336: simulate_douady_couder_hofmeister(): Hofmeister repulsive energy minimization <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L274-L336>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "While Delaunay parastichy pairs and NND-CV behave properly near the golden angle, the independent audit discovered that compute_packing_metrics() clips Voronoi cell areas to 0.05 < area < 20.0, allowing degenerate rational 120 deg spokes to report a lower voronoi_cv_area (0.000314) than the golden angle (0.0445), and Panel C's CV labels were hardcoded strings inconsistent with the CSV. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L215–L267: compute_packing_metrics(): area filter lets degenerate 120 deg lattice score 0.000314 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L215-L267>; vogel_phyllotaxis_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): rational_120.0 row has voronoi_cv_area=0.000314 in v1 — vogel_phyllotaxis_metrics.csv: rendered output of 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py at c89d18d, text/csv, 317 B, artifact_sha256 6f49a262bb096f0224a616c0d5df079ce4277b3b324c4abde34c661191bfecf4 (sha256 6f49a262bb096f0224a616c0d5df079ce4277b3b324c4abde34c661191bfecf4), spec_fingerprint 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): golden divergence angle α₀ = 360°/τ² = 137.5078 degrees (reference 137.50776405003785, Vogel 1979 Mathematical Biosciences 44:179 Eq. (1)-(4)) [exact golden-section divergence angle 360 * (2 - τ)]; outer-annulus [14.5, 22.5) opposed contact parastichy ratio (n/m) = 1.6177 ratio (55/34) (reference 1.61765, Vogel 1979 / Swinton et al. 2016 R. Soc. Open Sci. 3:160091 §2.3) [Delaunay contact parastichy pair (34, 55) in outer annulus r in [14.5, 22.5)] — full radial cascade: [(8, 13), (13, 21), (21, 34), (34, 55)]; Voronoi cell area CV at golden angle (137.5078°) = 0.0072 CV (std/mean) (reference 0.009777076602327022, Vogel 1979 Fig. 2a negative control (α = 137.30°)) [Voronoi polygon area dispersion across interior florets (0.18 R_max <= r <= 0.85 R_max, N=450)] — strictly lower than α=137.30° (0.0098) and α=137.60° (0.0074); Douady & Couder (1992) Hofmeister main-branch emergent divergence angle = 137.586 degrees (reference 137.507764, Douady & Couder 1992 Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098 Fig. 3) [mean steady-state divergence angle over final 25 plastochrons on main Fibonacci branch (G: 0.55 -> 0.04)]; Douady & Couder (1992) Hofmeister Lucas-branch emergent divergence angle = 99.38 degrees (reference 99.501553, Douady & Couder 1992 Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098 / 1996 J. Theor. Biol. 178:255) [mean steady-state divergence angle over final 25 plastochrons on secondary Lucas branch (G: 0.22 -> 0.04)]; Swinton et al. (2016) photoreviewed Fibonacci-structure prevalence = 82.29 percent (reference 82.29, Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium 2016 R. Soc. Open Sci. 3:160091 Table 1) [632 of 768 photoreviewed Helianthus annuus parastichy counts belonging to Fibonacci, Lucas, Double-Fib, or F4 sequences] — Fib-1 (49) vs Fib+1 (17) one-sided binomial p = 5.07e-05." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — MorphoEval overall 64.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Initial v1 implementation of Vogel (1979) golden-angle phyllotaxis and Douady & Couder (1992) Hofmeister inhibitory dynamics, paired with Swinton et al. (2016) Royal Society Helianthus annuus survey tables and two Wikimedia Commons specimen photographs. Independent audit by Claude Sonnet 5.5 High scored v1 at 64.3 overall, surfacing four concrete bugs and missing measurements targeted for Step 12 remediation. Overall 64.3/100 (faithfulness 59.6, reproducibility 75.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 55, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 80, Code-to-model traceability 66, Reproducibility package 78. Output judged: vogel_phyllotaxis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py at c89d18d, image/png, 2155516 B, 2960×1840 px, artifact_sha256 98e2578361a0d0405b5a71cddc2f9ada03e666fcfb80e10ed5b14086a937b07d (sha256 98e2578361a0d0405b5a71cddc2f9ada03e666fcfb80e10ed5b14086a937b07d), spec_fingerprint 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c; artifact_sha256: 98e2578361a0d0405b5a71cddc2f9ada03e666fcfb80e10ed5b14086a937b07d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/phyllotaxis/helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg=c76483eea3e564fe..., datasets/phyllotaxis/helianthus_parastichy_annotated.jpg=7cd34354e23584cb..., datasets/phyllotaxis/phyllotaxis_reference.json=432d1eeebf62bdc7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Vogel (1979) defines planar capitulum spiral placement r_n = c*sqrt(n), theta_n = n*alpha_0 with golden divergence angle alpha_0 = 360/tau^2 = 137.507764 deg | Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) demonstrate self-organized convergence of repulsive Hofmeister primordia on a radially advecting meristem ring to the golden and Lucas noble angles | Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium (2016) report 768 photoreviewed parastichy counts across 657 Helianthus annuus heads (82.3% Fibonacci structure; 49 Fib-1 vs 17 Fib+1, binomial p = 3.3e-5); reconstructed_in_script: Planar Vogel spiral generator, Delaunay/Voronoi contact parastichy detector across concentric annuli, quasi-static Douady-Couder Hofmeister relaxation, and Swinton (2016) empirical survey comparison; transfer_boundary: Noisy divergence ensemble and bijugate whorl extensions used to compare model parastichy distributions with Swinton et al. (2016) Table 1; does_not_claim: In v1, floret centroids/parastichy modes are not yet extracted from the specimen photograph pixels, and Fib-1/Fib+1 grain defects are not yet produced by the noisy simulation ensemble." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extract quantitative morphometrics (2D polar/radial Fourier parastichy spectrum and detected floret centroids) directly from the empirical specimen photograph (`helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg` and `helianthus_parastichy_annotated.jpg`) and compare against the Vogel model.",
        "remediation needed: Fix `compute_packing_metrics()` so degenerate rational angles (e.g. 120 deg) are penalized by bounding the Capitulum disk (or using bounded Voronoi / NND + angular coverage uniformity) so the golden angle is a true global optimum across [90 deg, 170 deg], and format Panel C CV labels dynamically from the computed metrics.",
        "remediation needed: Fix all code-traceability mismatches found by the second assessor (Panel E legend initial angles, Sunflower 171 (47,76) outer zone, F4 vs Fib+1 classification of 14, and BibTeX entries for Schoute 1938, Weisse 1897, and Jean 1994).",
        "remediation needed: Model and test the Swinton et al. (2016) Fib-1 > Fib+1 grain-defect asymmetry mechanistically (via plastochron/radial transition-zone noise on finite capitula where outer-rim parastichy transitions are Incomplete by 1 spiral more often than supernumerary by 1 spiral) and report chi-square / binomial agreement against Table 1." ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.43e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Parameter expressivity: 68/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Divergence angle alpha_deg, floret count n_florets, jugacy J, and plastochron schedule G_start/G_end are parameterized and swept across Panels B, C, D, and E. However, angular/radial noise sigma is not systematically swept and no parameter regime is shown generating the empirical Fib-1 > Fib+1 grain-defect asymmetry. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L659–L686: Panel C 2x2 parameter comparison across 137.3, 137.6, 99.502, and bijugate J=2 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L659-L686>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L691–L703: Panel D alpha_scan across [136.6, 138.4] deg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L691-L703>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Reproducibility package: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Self-contained script with --self-test, deterministic RNG seeds, verified dataset image SHA-256 checks, static PNG, animated GIF, and CSV outputs. Can be improved by hashing phyllotaxis_reference.json and reporting output digests directly. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L375–L474: run_self_tests() verifying SHA-256, cascade, and convergence <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L375-L474>; docs/media/vogel_phyllotaxis_growth.gif (generated output, not in repo): Animated growth GIF — docs/media/vogel_phyllotaxis_growth.gif: rendered output of 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py at c89d18d, image/gif, 877508 B, 1120×540 px, 27 frames, artifact_sha256 8e8d60ceff1e2574ef41906e7f2dabc2a47ce15029dc16d80519dcee4f693897 (sha256 8e8d60ceff1e2574ef41906e7f2dabc2a47ce15029dc16d80519dcee4f693897), spec_fingerprint 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Source and data traceability: 80/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "DOIs for Vogel (1979), Douady & Couder (1992, 1996), Swinton et al. (2016), and Dryad (10.5061/dryad.f9k77) are recorded in phyllotaxis_reference.json and paper_citations.bib, and both Wikimedia Commons photographs have verified SHA-1 and SHA-256 digests. Historical surveys (Schoute 1938, Weisse 1897, Jean 1994) should also be added to paper_citations.bib. Evidence: datasets/phyllotaxis/phyllotaxis_reference.json L1–L135: DOIs, equations, SHA-256 locks, and Swinton (2016) Tables 1-4 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/datasets/phyllotaxis/phyllotaxis_reference.json#L1-L135>; datasets/phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib L1–L41: BibTeX citations with DOIs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/datasets/phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib#L1-L41>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-vogel-phyllotaxis-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 55/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Two real CC-licensed Helianthus annuus capitulum photographs are vendored and displayed in Panel A with verified SHA-256 digests, and Swinton et al.'s (2016) 768 photoreviewed parastichy counts are plotted in Panel F. However, in v1 the specimen photograph is only shown via imshow() without pixel/Fourier parastichy extraction, and the simulated ensemble produces 0% Fib-1 and Fib+1 defects. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L552–L581: Panel A displays helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg and annotated inset <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L552-L581>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L778–L804: Panel F noisy Vogel ensemble yields 0% Fib-1 and Fib+1 in v1 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L778-L804>; vogel_phyllotaxis_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): 6-panel comparison figure — vogel_phyllotaxis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py at c89d18d, image/png, 2155516 B, 2960×1840 px, artifact_sha256 98e2578361a0d0405b5a71cddc2f9ada03e666fcfb80e10ed5b14086a937b07d (sha256 98e2578361a0d0405b5a71cddc2f9ada03e666fcfb80e10ed5b14086a937b07d), spec_fingerprint 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

